    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d162">

                <pb facs="0204" n="1038" xml:id="pg1038"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72112/9888</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jay</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Rome</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-08-23T12:00:00+02:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 23, 1918, 12 noon.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 24, 2.11
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1948. War Trade Board, Bureau Enemy Trade [from Stewart]:</p>
                <p>No. 2. Referring your No. 163, July 2, to McFadden.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d162-f1"
                    /> At his request have conferred with Italian Foreign Office in regard to
                    acceptance by Italy of War Trade Board resolution of April 29, concerning enemy
                    trading license committees. Am now advised that Italy will accept principle of
                    this resolution but acceptance is limited to licenses for trading with listed
                    persons. Italy will submit such applications to proposed committees but will not
                    agree to submit applications for licenses to trade with enemy persons not
                    listed. Stewart.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jay</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
